Use case: precise-object-edit. Asset type: transparent chibi Spine texture attachment sheet. Image 1 is the EDIT TARGET: a 4-column by 4-row grid of isolated existing character parts, currently on gray with labels. Image 2 is the REFERENCE for Chen Qianyu's hair, eyes and horns. Return the same 4x4 fixed-cell layout with transparent background; remove all labels and grid lines. Change only these colors/details, not the shapes or orientations: hair must become softer lighter charcoal-black / slate-gray black with muted neutral gray highlights, NOT deep navy-black or purple. All four horns keep blue mids and dark pointed tips but add visible rosy pink/magenta only at their broad bottom roots where they meet the hair. The pair of eyes in row 1 column 1 must keep gray/silver irises and the current cute chibi style, with a distinctly thin VERTICAL RED SLIT PUPIL in the center of EACH gray iris, plus the existing white shine; do NOT make solid red irises. Preserve both eyes as two separated pieces in that cell, in precisely the original relative positions. Preserve every attachment's original silhouette, scale within its cell, facing, shading logic and transparency holes. Back-of-head hair includes a tiny skin-colored nape: preserve that skin.
Cell order, left to right:
row1 F_Eyes, F_B_Hair, F_F_Hair, F_L_Hair;
row2 F_R_Hair_A, F_R_Hair_B, F_L_Braid, F_R_Braid;
row3 F_L_Horn, F_R_Horn, B_Head, B_F_Hair;
row4 B_L_Braid, B_R_Braid, B_L_Horn, B_R_Horn.
No additional body, garment, face, hands, weapon, background, words, labels, glows or new parts. These are production UV pieces, not a character illustration.
